{
  "format": 1,
  "name": "aura_landmark_funding",
  "spec": ["aura 6", "aura 6.3", "aura 17.3", "foundations 18.1"],
  "description": "State 3, one department per call in ascending ID: A (0x10, funding 0.5, value 30) gives trunc(15) = 15; B (0x20, 1.2, value 10) gives trunc(15 + 12.0) = 27; the third call publishes 27 and moves to 4 (N + 1 calls). Negative values are not scaled: -8, then trunc(-8 + 3 x 1.2) = trunc(-4.4) = -4. Department ID 0 uses 1.0 even with a funding entry (1 + 15 + 12 = 28; value 7 kept). A cursor naming a department that does not exist resets the cursor and moves to 4 without publishing (the map keeps its previous values). f32 steps per foundations 18; values from a Python model. int16 stores keep the low 16 bits of _ftol (6 'Integer stores', [compat]): two departments 0x30 and 0x40 with value 20000 each at funding 1.0 -> first 20000, then trunc(float32(20000 + 20000)) = 40000, stored as -25536 (wrap, not 32767), and the landmark map is -25536.",
